 "poem": "The damsel of the Isaurian elevation\nShee dropt her eyes, and fell with soft hesitation.\nIt was quite preposterous explanation,\nAt least to me it seemed so; explanation,\nNo word in my writing could imitate.\n'And now, then,' she answered faintly, she\n'Speak, speak at all!' [6] and I went away.\nThen came an idle dream. There suddenly\nBefore my vision stood a incarnation\nIn paradise: - 'Oh! do not hesitation!\nHe spake but one long sentence, which conversation\nCould never take; he spoke thus someone",
